window.docContents[254].resolve({"/8___-Homological-algebra/8___2___-Tor-and-Ext-functors/Ext-functors/#Chapter8___Definition8___2___4":{"contents":"Definition 8.2.4. Let M be a left A-module, P_\\bullet a projective resolution of M, and N a left A-module. For i \\geq 0 we define \\mathrm{Ext}^i_A(M, N) = \\mathrm{Ext}^i(M, N) to be the ith cohomology of the complex\n\n0 \\to \\mathrm{Hom}_A(P_0, N) \\to \\mathrm{Hom}_A(P_1, N) \\to \\mathrm{Hom}_A(P_2, N) \\to \\ldots\n\ninduced by the resolution P_\\bullet.\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t8. Homological algebra\t8.2. Tor and Ext functors\tExt functors","header":"Ext functors","id":"/8___-Homological-algebra/8___2___-Tor-and-Ext-functors/Ext-functors/#Chapter8___Definition8___2___4"},"/8___-Homological-algebra/8___2___-Tor-and-Ext-functors/Computing-Tor-and-Ext-for-abelian-groups-and-polynomial-modules/#Chapter8___Problem8___2___7":{"contents":"Problem 8.2.7. (i) Let A = \\mathbb{Z} and let M, N be finitely generated abelian groups. Compute \\operatorname{Tor}_i(M, N), \\operatorname{Ext}^i(M, N) (Hint: Reduce to the case of cyclic groups using the classification theorem for finite abelian groups.)\n\n(ii) Do the same for A = k[x] and M, N being any finitely generated A-modules.\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t8. Homological algebra\t8.2. Tor and Ext functors\tComputing Tor and Ext for abelian groups and polynomial modules","header":"Computing Tor and Ext for abelian groups and polynomial modules","id":"/8___-Homological-algebra/8___2___-Tor-and-Ext-functors/Computing-Tor-and-Ext-for-abelian-groups-and-polynomial-modules/#Chapter8___Problem8___2___7"}});
